Subject: [PATCH 1/2] isaspec: allow <param>s on derived fields of bitset type

A <derived> field may have a bitset type, so that a sub-encoding whose
bits are scattered across the instruction can be put together by an
expression and decoded by one bitset hierarchy. Such a field needs
<param>s like a plain bitset field: parse them, and add their names to
the encoder's bitset_params struct.

The SGX545 instruction set description is the first user. The code
generated for ir3, etnaviv and qrisc doesn't change.
---
