From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:13:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] isaspec: encode: stop at the override that defines the
 field

Inside the branch for an <override> that defines a field, the encoder
also emitted that field's definitions from the overrides after it, as an
if/else ladder. The ladder has no final else of its own, so the code for
the next field became its else: when the expression of one of the later
overrides holds too, the next field isn't encoded, and a later override's
definition is OR'ed into the word.

The decoder uses the first override whose expression holds, so make the
encoder stop at the case being encoded, too.

ir3's overrides of a field test exclusive conditions, so its encoder only
loses unreachable code (120 lines of the generated encode.h). etnaviv's
and qrisc's generated code doesn't change. The SGX545 instruction set
description has overlapping overrides and needs the fix.
